1
00:00:01,668 --> 00:00:05,271
8：30了，8：00的校车10分钟后就要到了
It's 8:30, guys. The 8:00 bus will be here in 10 minutes.

2
00:00:05,271 --> 00:00:06,966
我还没准备好
And I still gotta get ready.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,260
我还没准备好
Ben. School.

4
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:12,120
忘了给你们，家长联谊会邀请
本，上学了
Forgot to give you guys this. It's a letter from the Parents Association.

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,640
凯罗，这没什么意思的
Ixnay on the etterlay, Carol.

6
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,180
-给我 -我来看看
- I'll take it. - Let me see that.

7
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:21,520
“贵家长，学校的每周舞会无法进行下去”
"Dear fellow parents, our program of weekly dances is in jeopardy...

8
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,840
“因为有些家长没有履行他们的义务”
"owing to the fact that many of you have not fulfilled...

9
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:28,040
“没有陪同子女参加舞会”
"your parental responsibilities and made yourselves available for chaperoning.

10
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:32,900
“谁不来谁心中有数，更重要的是 我们心中有数”
"You know who you are and, more importantly, we know who you are.

11
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:36,040
“敬礼，家长联谊会主席..”
"Sincerely, Mrs. Adolf Hitler."

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,820
“琼.亨克利，阿道夫老师” 很友善的一对信
"June Hinckley, President of the Parents Association." Nice tone.

13
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:45,380
爸妈都那么忙.
Now, come on now, busy people like you guys have far better things to do...

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,640
哪有空去体育馆那种脏地方
than to hang around a smelly gym.

15
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,900
-让麦克丢脸 -对
- Embarrassing Mike. - Yeah.

16
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,040
不，不
I mean, no.

17
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:52,960
丢脸？
Embarrass?

18
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:54,860
妈妈，这是她说的
That was her word, not my word, Mom.

19
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:59,040
我不介意爸妈出席舞会
I don't care if they chaperone dances. Bye.

20
00:00:59,859 --> 00:01:02,432
因为你从来没参加过舞会
That's 'cause you've never been to one.

21
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:04,900
麦克，这种信以前也有过？
Mike, did you get one of these letters?

22
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:06,540
来过
Yeah, sure.

23
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,560
在哪？
Well? Where is it?

24
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:12,160
妈妈拜托你相信我
Come on, Mom. Give me some kind of credit here.

25
00:01:12,539 --> 00:01:15,420
我是不想用这破玩意儿麻烦你们
Look, I'm not gonna bother you guys with a stupid letter like that.

26
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:17,560
我帮你们筛选过了
Look, I try to screen these things for you guys.

27
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:20,660
丢弃垃圾邮件
You know, you know, cut down on the junk mail...

28
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,040
节约你们宝贵的时间
protect your valuable time.

29
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,260
都丢到厕所里面去了
It's stuck to the ceiling in the boys' john.

30
00:01:28,236 --> 00:01:31,725
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E16 -= The.Seavers.VS.The.Cleavers =- Subripped by zerox

31
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,120
-本，上车 -不去就赶不上了
- Ben, the bus. - Use it or lose it.

32
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:36,100
本，你花太多的时间学习.
Come on, Ben, I think you're spending far too much time studying...

33
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:37,800
都没时间去玩了
and not nearly enough horsing around.

34
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:38,640
Hey!

35
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:42,380
本知道老爸在说笑，对吧？
I'm kidding. Ben knows when the old dad is kidding. Right, Ben?

36
00:02:42,762 --> 00:02:43,997
是，老爷
Aye, milord.

37
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:45,060
“是，老爷”？
"Aye, milord"?

38
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,840
这是<罗宾汉>里的台词 学校今年的舞台剧
It's from Robin Hood. That's the school play this year.

39
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:51,860
所以叫我“老爷”不是出于尊重
You mean you weren't calling me "milord" as a measure of respect?

40
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:56,460
这才有意思嘛
That's funny, Dad.

41
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:00,120
爸爸是跟你开玩笑
See, he does know when his old dad's kidding.

42
00:03:00,547 --> 00:03:03,120
今年我要参演
This year I'm going to get a part.

43
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,960
记得去年你没被选上，心都碎了
Well, let's hope, but I remember last year's auditions, how heartbroken you were.

44
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,840
行了爸爸，去年我还小呢
Come on, Dad. I was just a kid.

45
00:03:09,422 --> 00:03:12,540
这么说你成了3年级唯一的大人.
Oh, I see. So this year as the only adult in the third grade...

46
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:13,480
你有优势
you ought to have a big edge.

47
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,080
就是这样
That's how I figure it.

48
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:16,380
祝你好运
Now good luck.

49
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:17,260
再见了
Bye, honey.

50
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:20,500
马到成功!
Break a leg!

51
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:22,400
什么？
What?

52
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,140
这是成语
Figure of speech.

53
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:30,100
杰森.
Jason...

54
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:33,160
你在麦克这个年纪.
when you were Mike's age would you have been afraid...

55
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:35,260
父母陪同参加舞会，你感到丢脸吗？
or embarrassed to have your parents chaperone?

56
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,240
对，我也经历过
Oh, sure. I went through that stage.

57
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:40,180
我父亲自告奋勇陪我参加学校活动
My dad volunteered to chaperone one of our class trips.

58
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,500
我就求他别去了
I begged him not to.

59
00:03:41,854 --> 00:03:43,680
我说，“爸爸，我不会干些出格的事”
I said, "Dad, but I'm not going to do anything."

60
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:46,260
他说“那就好，有我在”
He said, "Well, that's fine. Then you can not do it with me there."

61
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,420
爸，气色挺好的 妈，你也是
Hey, looking good, Dad. Vicious ensemble, Mom.

62
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:56,174
-住你们今天愉快 -且慢!
- You both have a nice day, now, you hear? - Halt!

63
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:58,440
妈，我要错过校车了
Mom, I might miss that darn bus.

64
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,580
打开拉链
Open the coat.

65
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:10,300
酷吧？
Is this cool or what?

66
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:14,240
麦克，穿成这样能上学吗？
Mike, do you really think you've dressed appropriately for school?

67
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:16,540
不，怎么能这样？
Heck, no. Why would I want to do that?

68
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,900
-换衣服 -爸？
- Change now. - Dad?

69
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:23,280
麦克，若你真的认为.
Mike. Now, Mike, if you think that this conveys...

70
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:26,820
这能代表你和家人的形象
the proper image, not just for yourself, but for the family you represent...

71
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:30,620
那么你完全可以挂一个鸡头出去
then, by all means, go ahead and wear a rubber fowl on your stomach.

72
00:04:32,338 --> 00:04:33,744
再见
See you.

73
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:35,460
杰森
Jason.

74
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:39,820
不知道为什么，热死了
I don't know why that works, but it's really starting to burn me up.

75
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:48,420
开学才一天 你不能因此断定学校不好
You know, you shouldn't judge the school by the first day.

76
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:51,900
而且你要体谅那些普通人
And you have to overlook all the average people.

77
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,460
这只是所公立学校
It is a public school.

78
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,740
这个我习来惯了
Well, I'm used to that, Carol.

79
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:01,760
洛杉矶也有许多普通人
You'd be surprised how many average people there are in Los Angeles.

80
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:07,440
我的自然老师甚至不许我做.
My old science teacher wouldn't even let me build a small model...

81
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,720
高热原子核的实验
of a thermonuclear device for a science project.

82
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:13,840
-裂变还是聚变？ -当然是聚变
- Fission or fusion? - Oh, fusion, of course.

83
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:14,500
“当然是”
Of course.

84
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:17,360
我打算要适应这里
I plan to fit in at this school.

85
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,940
我还加入了舞会组织委员会
I've already joined the dance decoration committee.

86
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:21,580
Oh?

87
00:05:22,889 --> 00:05:26,826
那么你会参加明晚的舞会？
Will you be at the dance then tomorrow night?

88
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:28,507
对
Sure.

89
00:05:28,761 --> 00:05:31,909
那你会跳舞？
Will you be dancing?

90
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:36,820
还没决定，也许当观察员
I haven't made up my mind yet. I might just observe.

91
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,400
嗨，麦克
Hi, Mike.

92
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:43,312
嗨，臭嘴巴
Hey, skunk-breath.

93
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:45,640
我哥哥
Brother.

94
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,940
麦克，是你吗？
Mike, is that you?

95
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,820
什么事？
What'd I do?

96
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,220
没什么
Nothing.

97
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:01,840
怎么样？
What do you think?

98
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,500
-很像你 -对
- It's you, Dad. - Yeah.

99
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,100
我的病人也这么说
That's what all the patients said.

100
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:11,340
爸爸!听我说.
Dad, Dad! Wait till you...

101
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,620
这里
Up here, Ben.

102
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,060
爸爸，我被选上了
Dad, I got a part! I got cast!

103
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,013
太好了!
Hey, all right! Good for you!

104
00:06:21,013 --> 00:06:22,648
演什么角色？罗宾汉的部将？
What'd you get? One of Robin's merry men?

105
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:23,300
不
Nope.

106
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,980
-修道士？ -不，更好的
- Friar Tuck? - Nope. Better.

107
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,540
-罗宾汉？ -不，更好的
- Not Robin? - No, better.

108
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:30,800
-什么？ -演一块石头
- What? - A rock.

109
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:33,820
一块石头？
A rock?

110
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,660
一块英国石头
An English rock.

111
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:40,300
希望演舞台据.
Well, I hope the hours required rehearsing this part...

112
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:41,500
不会影响你的功课
won't interfere with your studies.

113
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,640
好就好在这
That's the best part.

114
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:45,620
我可以上台，参加派对.
I can be in the play...

115
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:49,140
而我只需要躺着不动就行了
go to all the parties and all I have to do is lay there.

116
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,860
我的石头儿子
My son, the rock.

117
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:53,060
对!
Yeah!

118
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,560
杰森，下面说说这件汗衫
Now, Jason, I want to talk to you about this shirt.

119
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:00,280
这形象不仅代表你
Now, if this is the proper image you wish to convey...

120
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,700
还代表你的家人
not only for yourself, but for the family you represent.

121
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,940
好吧
Okay, all right.

122
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:06,220
真可惜
All right, it's a shame, though.

123
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:10,640
我还以为能穿这个陪你参加舞会
I was thinking of wearing this when your mom and I chaperone your school dance.

124
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,140
什么？
What?

125
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:15,220
你们真的要去舞会？
You're not really going to chaperone?

126
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:16,860
骗你们的
Had you going there for a second, didn't I?

127
00:07:19,672 --> 00:07:21,719
-太好啊 -是啊
- Put it there. - Yeah.

128
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:25,300
等等，怎么了？
Hey, wait a minute. What's this?

129
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:26,920
-什么事？ -什么事？
- What? - What?

130
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,800
你们俩平生第一次一个鼻孔出气了
For the first time in your lives, you two agree on something.

131
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:31,260
这才像样
That's better.

132
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,120
我还以为你不在乎家长陪同出席呢
I thought you said you didn't care whether they chaperoned or not.

133
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:38,000
不在乎，真的
I don't. Really.

134
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,340
凯罗，你从来不去舞会
Carol, you don't even go to these dances.

135
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:44,920
说不定这次会，我还没决定
Well, I might go to this one. I'm keeping my options open.

136
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:48,480
她想去是因为门口那书呆子也去
She just wants to go because that geek out on the front porch wants to go.

137
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:51,820
他不是书呆子，他刚从洛杉矶转学过来
He's not a geek. He's from Los Angeles.

138
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,440
凯罗，你在他面前都喘气了
You're breathing heavy for him, Carol.

139
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:02,260
才不是，我们在讨论核武器
I am not. We were discussing nuclear weapons.

140
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,080
听见了吧？没什么的
See? Perfectly harmless.

141
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:08,940
你害怕爸妈陪同出席
Carol, you're just afraid that if Mom and Dad chaperone...

142
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:11,760
你就不能化妆，不能跳贴身舞.
you won't be able to wear makeup and go slow dancing...

143
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,940
也不能偷偷溜到停车场去
and run off into the parking lot with that goon.

144
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:14,820
麦克!
Michael!

145
00:08:15,394 --> 00:08:20,105
停车场？我的女儿？喘气？
Parking lot? My little girl? Heavy breathing?

146
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,620
洛杉矶？
Los Angeles?

147
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:23,780
别听他的
Don't listen to him, Dad.

148
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:26,320
父母陪同出席并没有错
You know, chaperoning is not all bad.

149
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:27,680
什么？
What?

150
00:08:28,207 --> 00:08:30,814
爸爸，我不会干出格的事
Dad, I'm not going to do anything.

151
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:33,700
很好，有我在
Fine. Then you can not do it with me there.

152
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,480
想打我就打吧
If you want to hit me, I won't stop you.

153
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:50,180
瞧，我知道不能穿这个
See? I knew it. I can't wear this.

154
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,680
家长应该穿得大方得体，而且要庸俗
Chaperones are supposed to look stodgy and respectable.

155
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:54,500
那这件怎样？
Well, then why don't you wear this one?

156
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,840
这件衣服庸俗？
You think that dress is stodgy?

157
00:08:58,840 --> 00:08:59,760
这件？
This one?

158
00:09:01,607 --> 00:09:03,500
庸俗？开玩笑的
Stodgy? I'm kidding.

159
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:06,000
我最喜欢这件了
I love this dress. It's my favorite dress.

160
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,640
做梦都梦见你穿呢
I have dreams about this dress.

161
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:08,940
好吧
Okay.

162
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,600
我还没来得及告诉你.
Oh, sweetheart, I haven't had the chance to tell you how surprised...

163
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:17,060
你改变主意 愿、意出席舞会是成熟的表现
and happy I was that you changed your mind and agreed to do this.

164
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,900
我很高兴
It shows real maturity.

165
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:22,920
我虽然成熟，但童心未泯
Well, that's me. Mature, yet curiously juvenile.

166
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:28,580
你不是因为凯罗所以去的
And, of course, the fact that Carol's going had nothing to do with it.

167
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:29,260
凯罗？
Carol who?

168
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:32,400
不说了
It's okay. It's okay.

169
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:36,320
你越是保守，我越喜欢
I love you when you're hopelessly old-fashioned.

170
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:44,140
我们明晚就是要看管好.
You realize this is exactly the sort of behavior we're supposed...

171
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:45,460
这种行为
to prevent tomorrow night.

172
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:48,540
但这是今晚
But this is tonight.

173
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:55,640
生活真奇妙，昨天第一次见面.
Isn't life crazy? I mean, I meet you for the first time yesterday...

174
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:58,060
后来发现我们都参加了组织委员会
and then I find out that we're on the same decorating committee.

175
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,940
真奇妙
Crazy, crazy, crazy.

176
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,760
我父母今晚要来
My parents are chaperoning tonight.

177
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,760
太遗憾了
I'm sorry.

178
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:12,180
谢谢你，这消息来得太突然了
Thank you. It came as quite a shock.

179
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:15,420
可以理解，我父母也试过
I can imagine. My parents chaperoned once.

180
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:17,000
如何？
How was it?

181
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,360
太可怕了
It was mortifying.

182
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:21,464
他们
They...

183
00:10:21,587 --> 00:10:23,661
凯罗，他们也跳舞了
Carol, they danced.

184
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:28,280
天哪!
Oh, my God!

185
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:34,000
我爸手舞足蹈，像打麦机一样
My father started flailing his arms like some huge thrashing machine.

186
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,520
我妈欢蹦乱跳的.
My mother, she kind of hopped and clapped...

187
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,180
还跟着音乐欢呼
and yelled "Hey" in time to the music.

188
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:43,680
真是恶梦
What a nightmare.

189
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,360
沃德？
Ward?

190
00:10:50,883 --> 00:10:52,298
阿道夫老师
Mrs. Hinckley.

191
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,780
你又为学校争光了
You've done our school proud, as usual.

192
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,580
谢谢
Thank you, Ward.

193
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:59,820
若是家长联谊会的女士们都像你.
If all the ladies in the Parents Association were like you...

194
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:01,220
那我的生活就妙极了
it would sure change my life.

195
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,080
谢谢
Thank you.

196
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:07,780
你给家长的信，写得很好
We loved your chaperone letter. It really did the trick.

197
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:10,580
太好了，今晚有家长来了？
Wonderful. Who is chaperoning tonight?

198
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:11,260
西弗家
The Seavers.

199
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:12,960
沃德
Ward?

200
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:14,220
什么事？
Yes?

201
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:16,060
没什么
I don't know.

202
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:20,680
也许为人父的在家里执业 做心理治疗是可以的
Maybe it's okay for a man to run a psychiatric practice out of the home...

203
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,860
也许在孩子们最需要时.
and maybe it's all right for a woman to go back to work...

204
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:26,040
为人母的到外面工作是可以的
just when her children need her most.

205
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:30,720
也许放纵孩子是可以的
And maybe letting our offspring run wild is hunky-dory.

206
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,880
也许是我太老派
And maybe I'm just old-fashioned.

207
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:35,300
也许吧
Could be.

208
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:36,880
沃德.
Ward.

209
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,360
我是怕西弗家.
Ward, I'm worried about the Seavers.

210
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:45,660
出席舞会的家长.
I mean, the type of people we need for chaperones...

211
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,880
应该是能控制自己子女的家长
should be able to control their own children.

212
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,860
这个要求还真不低
Wow, that's a pretty high standard.

213
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,800
你父母也许更糟糕
Boy, your parents sound worse than mine.

214
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:10,060
-亲爱的 -你提早回家了
- Hi, honey. - Hi. You're home early.

215
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:11,640
今天新闻不多
Slow news day.

216
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,180
老爷和太太都回到宫殿了
Oh, well then the lord and lady of the manor...

217
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:15,900
他们的二人世界
have the castle all to themselves.

218
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,300
大家好
Hey, guys, how you doing?

219
00:12:20,456 --> 00:12:21,320
我去接
I'll get that.

220
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:24,220
该死的，我不演了
That does it, I quit the play.

221
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:28,040
你终于不去当那块石头了？
Ben, you're not going to be a rock after all?

222
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:29,160
不干了
No way.

223
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:32,780
第二场修道士一直坐在我身上
Friar Tuck sits on me all through Act 2.

224
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:38,982
好吧，我们下次再当监督人
Well, that's okay then, we can chaperone another time.

225
00:12:40,376 --> 00:12:42,986
谢谢希特勒..阿道夫老师
Well, thank you for calling, Mrs. Hitler... Hinckley.

226
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,680
好，再见
All right. Bye.

227
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,920
-你们不出席了？ -不去了
- You mean we aren't chaperoning? - No.

228
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:52,000
快掐掐我，不是做梦吧？ 太好了
Somebody pinch me. I'm dreaming. This is great.

229
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:55,180
不是这样的
No, it's not.

230
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,040
你疯了？
What are you, nuts?

231
00:12:57,493 --> 00:12:59,840
我全知道了
Forget it, I already know the answer.

232
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,400
她告诉你原因了吗？
Did she tell you why?

233
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:04,620
这个星期的监督人请重复了
Well, apparently they've double-booked the chaperones this week.

234
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:06,940
她骗你的
Well, she lied to you.

235
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:11,420
不请你们是因为.
The reason you're not chaperoning is because...

236
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:12,920
你们是不合格的父母
you're unacceptable parents.

237
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,760
不合格的父母？
Unacceptable parents?

238
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:17,320
你亲耳听到的？
Carol, you heard this?

239
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,560
不单是我
Not just me.

240
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:21,580
斯柯蒂每个字都听到了
Scotty Siegler heard every word of it.

241
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:23,460
好极了!
All right!

242
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,680
我不明白
I don't get it.

243
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:30,540
她说我妈妈丢下我去工作
She said I have a mother who abandoned me...

244
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:33,440
哥哥是少年犯，爸爸在家开精神病院
a brother who's a delinquent, a father who runs a mental ward at home.

245
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,600
把我的生活说得像电影一样
She made my life sound like a Movie of the Week.

246
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:40,980
我宰了她
I'll kill her.

247
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,560
麦姬，别急
Maggie, don't get upset.

248
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:45,560
杰森，你怎能若无其事的？
Jason, how can you stand there so calmly?

249
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:49,440
其实我也深深感到愤怒
Actually, I have deeply rooted feelings of anger and hostility.

250
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:53,640
但是发脾气前我要核实一下 是否存在误解
I just refuse to give vent to them until we find out if there's some misunderstanding.

251
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,620
我可是要发脾气
I'll give her a vent.

252
00:13:56,151 --> 00:13:58,327
明天全校都会传开来了
This will be all over the school by tomorrow.

253
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,700
不会的，别人怎么会听到呢？
Oh, Carol, it will not. How's anybody going to hear?

254
00:14:00,823 --> 00:14:04,500
我没骗你，他们就是这么说的 “不合格”
No, man, I'm not kidding. That's what they said: "unacceptable."

255
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:07,540
等等，有电话进来了
All right, hold on. I have someone else on the other line.

256
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:09,340
麦克，这事没什么好炫耀的
Mike, this is nothing to brag about.

257
00:14:09,465 --> 00:14:11,378
我知道，喂？
I know, Dad. Hello?

258
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,980
杰里，你也听到了，对!
Oh, hi, Jerry. Oh, you heard. Yeah!

259
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:17,051
他们不允许我父母 接近学校1里范围内
They don't want my parents within a mile of that school.

260
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,960
我不要住在这城市了
I'll never live this down.

261
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:23,440
等等，昨天你们感到丢脸 是因为我们是合格的
Just a minute. Yesterday you were embarrassed because we were acceptable.

262
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:25,280
正是
Exactly.

263
00:14:25,860 --> 00:14:28,260
现在让我受多大的罪了？
Now do you see what you're putting me through?

264
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,240
真是离谱
This is absolutely unbelievable.

265
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:34,880
对，我们家是垃圾!
Yeah. We're garbage!

266
00:14:39,228 --> 00:14:41,402
-你答应过不发脾气的 -是的
- Do you promise to hold your temper? - Yes.

267
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,480
-骗我吧？ -是的
- Are you lying? - Yes.

268
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:52,880
来也，是西弗一家吗？
Hi-ho, you must be the Seavers.

269
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:54,840
我叫吉姆
Call me Jimbo.

270
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:56,480
来也
Hi-ho.

271
00:14:57,500 --> 00:15:00,460
进来，今晚有烧烤
Go on in. I have BBQ detail tonight.

272
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:14,260
瞧？都是有礼貌的人
See? These are reasonable people.

273
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:19,480
西弗先生，西弗太太
Mr. And Mrs. Seaver, how nice of you...

274
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,620
今日来访真是太客气了
to insist on dropping by.

275
00:15:22,705 --> 00:15:25,356
你好，我叫杰森
Yes, well, hello, my name's Jason.

276
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:34,660
你好，这到底是.
How do you do? Now what's all this crud about...

277
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,400
阿道夫老师，我们不会打扰你很久
We won't take up much of your time, Mrs. Hinckley.

278
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,820
只是想澄清一点误会
We just thought we should come by and clear up a little misunderstanding.

279
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,360
请坐下
Well, won't you sit down?

280
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:46,820
好的，谢谢
Yes, yes, we will. Thank you very much.

281
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:52,000
谣传你说过一些话.
Well, the thing is that we heard this crazy rumor that you said...

282
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,620
也许是搞错了
and this is probably all wrong...

283
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:58,800
听闻你说我们是不合格的家长
but that you said something about us being "unacceptable" parents.

284
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:03,720
这话不该传到你们耳朵那里
Oh, dear. I'm afraid that wasn't meant for your ears.

285
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,760
这么说真有其事？
So, you did say that?

286
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:08,820
是的
Oh, yes.

287
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:13,840
你干嘛要破坏我们的名誉？
Just where in the hell do you get off ruining our reputation?

288
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:16,360
我们家很少这样说话
We don't use that word in our home.

289
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:19,180
-该死的!你.. -“该死”也是
- Damn it! How can you... - Or that one.

290
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:22,840
我还有三个字要说呢
Well, I have two more words you won't like, June.

291
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:25,760
什么？
Yes?

292
00:16:26,001 --> 00:16:28,981
没什么，一下子头脑发热了
No, no... Now, I'm getting carried away here.

293
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:31,480
杰森，没关系，说吧
It's okay, Jason, get carried away.

294
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,308
不，我们是来.
No, no. I would like to make one more attempt...

295
00:16:33,308 --> 00:16:35,377
-但.. -沟通沟通的
- But... ...at some real communication here.

296
00:16:35,377 --> 00:16:37,561
-我.. -斯波特？
- L... - Sport?

297
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:42,020
晚上出门.
When one goes out for an evening...

298
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,660
穿着要对得上场合
one dresses properly for the occasion.

299
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:48,832
-可是妈妈你.. -你知道我喜欢什么
- Oh, but, Mother... - You know what Mother likes.

300
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:50,420
疯婆子!
Nuts!

301
00:16:50,940 --> 00:16:51,860
什么？
Excuse me?

302
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:53,580
是，妈妈
Yes, Mother.

303
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:55,340
真是孩子气
Children.

304
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:59,440
咱们就开门见山吧
Hold on to your slipcovers, June, because I'm gonna...

305
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:01,280
麦姬，麦姬，这是怎么了？
Maggie, Maggie, Maggie, what's the point?

306
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:03,460
我们再待下去.
We're not on the same planet here.

307
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:05,800
这样能解决问题吗？
And if we stay any longer we're just going to make ourselves crazy.

308
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,680
对她骂出脏话来.
And we probably will end up hurling obscenities at this woman...

309
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:09,580
那又有什么好处呢？
and what would that accomplish?

310
00:17:13,715 --> 00:17:16,557
见鬼!试试看吧
Well, what the heck? Let's give it a shot.

311
00:17:18,086 --> 00:17:21,634
宝贝，汉堡包快好了
June bug, these burgers are very close.

312
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:36,200
Uh-oh.

313
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:38,880
嗨，本
Hi, Ben.

314
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:40,060
嗨
Hi.

315
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,300
哥哥呢？
Where's your brother?

316
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:42,280
去了舞会
At the dance.

317
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,320
-姐姐呢？ -在房间里
- Where's your sister? - In her room.

318
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:45,680
沙发呢？
Where's the couch?

319
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:48,440
不知道，刚才还在
I don't know. It was here a minute ago.

320
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,000
好吧，我来擦干净
Okay, I'll clean it up.

321
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:58,040
别擦!干脆翘个二郎腿
Don't clean it up! Don't be... Don't worry! Come here. Put those feet up here.

322
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:00,260
鞋子不用脱，这才像个孩子
Leave those shoes on. Be a kid.

323
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,820
这才是本
This is the way I like Ben.

324
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:05,480
又脏又懒的真正的孩子
Sloppy, lazy, a real kid.

325
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:08,860
若我们不是好家长 凯罗成绩会这么好吗？
And if we're such bad parents, how did Carol turn out so well?

326
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,720
对，还有麦克!十全十美
That's right. And Mike! Mike's perfect.

327
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:14,660
我丧失理智了
Okay, I lost my head.

328
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:18,780
谁也不能说我们教不好孩子
But the point is, nobody says we did a bad job raising our kids.

329
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:21,360
谁也不能禁止我们出席舞会
And nobody tells us we can't chaperone.

330
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:29,440
凯罗，快点，要错过舞会了
Carol? Hurry up! You're late for the dance.

331
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:32,480
我不去，太丢脸了
I'm not going. I'm too humiliated.

332
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:35,200
凯罗，没关系，我们也去
Carol, it's all right. We're chaperoning.

333
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:38,980
太好了，我要扬眉吐气了
Oh, great. My life is an acid bath.

334
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:41,760
换衣服吧
Let's change.

335
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:43,080
我去叫人看管本
I'll call the sitter.

336
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,460
爸爸，有好东西让你看
Hey, Dad, you're gonna love this.

337
00:19:10,499 --> 00:19:15,010
也许校规会禁止任何人跟我父母谈话
I wouldn't be surprised if they made it a crime just to talk to my parents.

338
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,640
这衣服可是选对了
Well, I guess you wore the right dress.

339
00:19:35,457 --> 00:19:37,169
坏了
Oh, nuts.

340
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:41,180
阿道夫!吉姆!
June! Jimbo!

341
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,740
Hey, hey, hey.

342
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,160
Hey, hey, hey.

343
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:45,260
挺热闹的
Nice dance.

344
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:50,040
你们来了也不等于是监督人
The fact that you're here doesn't make you chaperones.

345
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:55,200
你们来了不等于只有你们来了
And the fact that you're here doesn't mean you're here.

346
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:02,940
下面我们要对长辈们致敬
Okay, now let's go way back and do a little tribute to our ancestors.

347
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:05,300
这是老摇滚音乐
Here's some genuine fogy rock...

348
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:07,820
监督人也要跳
and that means our chaperones must dance.

349
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:14,840
监督人是你们吧？
Well, as you pointed out, you're the chaperones.

350
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,660
麦姬，怎么看？
Well, Maggie, what do you say?

351
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:40,040
我说.
I say...

352
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:57,700
我永远也不能回到这个学校了
I'll never be able to come back to this school again.

353
00:20:58,020 --> 00:21:00,720
不，这种污点过一两年就会淡去
No, don't worry. The stigma fades after a year or two.

354
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:06,180
其实你爸妈跳得不错
You know, actually, your parents aren't too bad. Look.

355
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,040
跳舞的是你父母吗？
Hey, are those your parents dancing?

356
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,880
不，我父母今晚没空
No, no. My parents couldn't make it tonight.

357
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,200
他们好像出国去了
They may have to leave the country.

358
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,220
是他们
Oh, no, that's them.

359
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,960
-谁？ -瞧他们跳得多棒
- Who? - The ones with all the moves.

360
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:28,820
你知道是谁教他们跳的吗？
Hey, hey, come on, who do you think showed them all those moves?

361
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:31,860
你父母还真酷呢
You know, your parents are reasonably cool.

362
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:34,860
当然，还用说
Sure, what'd you expect?

363
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:41,640
为第一名欢呼!
Let's hear it for couple number one!

364
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:49,020
为第二名欢呼!
And couple number two!

365
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:16,865
爸妈，这是斯柯蒂
Mom, Dad, this is Scotty Siegler.

366
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:17,640
-嗨 -嗨
- Hi. - Hi.

367
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:20,740
-他送我回家可以吗？ -可以
- Is it okay if he walks me home? - Sure.

368
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,180
爸爸你!
But, Dad!

369
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:24,340
Oh.

370
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:27,940
谢谢!
Okay. Thanks!

371
00:22:33,980 --> 00:22:34,860
好吧.
Okay. All right...

372
00:22:34,860 --> 00:22:38,380
今晚你们可以自由一点 但别得意忘形
you guys got away with it once. I don't want this to go to your heads.

373
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,300
妈，这套衣服也太火辣了
This is a hot dress, Mom.

374
00:22:41,676 --> 00:22:45,280
以后别在我朋友面前穿了
And please, don't ever wear it in front of my friends again.

375
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:47,762
麦克，回家去
Mike, go home.

376
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:53,080
我玩得很开心
Well, I had fun.

377
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,760
我也是
So did I.

378
00:22:55,257 --> 00:22:58,239
真的是老摇滚
Fogy rock, indeed.

379
00:22:58,827 --> 00:23:01,376
好吧，老家伙
Well, let's go, fogy.

380
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,380
摇滚吧
Let's rock.

381
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:54,023
